{"entryType": "UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)", "primaryAccession": "A0LLG1", "uniProtkbId": "ATPD_SYNFM", "entryAudit": {"firstPublicDate": "2009-05-05", "lastAnnotationUpdateDate": "2025-06-18", "lastSequenceUpdateDate": "2006-12-12", "entryVersion": 93, "sequenceVersion": 1}, "annotationScore": 2.0, "organism": {"scientificName": "Syntrophobacter fumaroxidans (strain DSM 10017 / MPOB)", "taxonId": 335543, "lineage": ["Bacteria", "Pseudomonadati", "Thermodesulfobacteriota", "Syntrophobacteria", "Syntrophobacterales", "Syntrophobacteraceae", "Syntrophobacter"]}, "proteinExistence": "3: Inferred from homology", "proteinDescription": {"recommendedName": {"fullName": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000255", "source": "HAMAP-Rule", "id": "MF_01416"}], "value": "ATP synthase subunit delta"}}, "alternativeNames": [{"fullName": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000255", "source": "HAMAP-Rule", "id": "MF_01416"}], "value": "ATP synthase F(1) sector subunit delta"}}, {"fullName": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000255", "source": "HAMAP-Rule", "id": "MF_01416"}], "value": "F-type ATPase subunit delta"}, "shortNames": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000255", "source": "HAMAP-Rule", "id": "MF_01416"}], "value": "F-ATPase subunit delta"}]}]}, "genes": [{"geneName": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000255", "source": "HAMAP-Rule", "id": "MF_01416"}], "value": "atpH"}, "orderedLocusNames": [{"value": "Sfum_2585"}]}], "comments": [{"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000255", "source": "HAMAP-Rule", "id": "MF_01416"}], "value": "F(1)F(0) ATP synthase produces ATP from ADP in the presence of a proton or sodium gradient. F-type ATPases consist of two structural domains, F(1) containing the extramembraneous catalytic core and F(0) containing the membrane proton channel, linked together by a central stalk and a peripheral stalk. During catalysis, ATP synthesis in the catalytic domain of F(1) is coupled via a rotary mechanism of the central stalk subunits to proton translocation"}], "commentType": "FUNCTION"}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000255", "source": "HAMAP-Rule", "id": "MF_01416"}], "value": "This protein is part of the stalk that links CF(0) to CF(1). It either transmits conformational changes from CF(0) to CF(1) or is implicated in proton conduction"}], "commentType": "FUNCTION"}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000255", "source": "HAMAP-Rule", "id": "MF_01416"}], "value": "F-type ATPases have 2 components, F(1) - the catalytic core - and F(0) - the membrane proton channel. F(1) has five subunits: alpha(3), beta(3), gamma(1), delta(1), epsilon(1). F(0) has three main subunits: a(1), b(2) and c(10-14). The alpha and beta chains form an alternating ring which encloses part of the gamma chain. F(1) is attached to F(0) by a central stalk formed by the gamma and epsilon chains, while a peripheral stalk is formed by the delta and b chains"}], "commentType": "SUBUNIT"}, {"commentType": "SUBCELLULAR LOCATION", "subcellularLocations": [{"location": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000255", "source": "HAMAP-Rule", "id": "MF_01416"}], "value": "Cell inner membrane", "id": "SL-0037"}, "topology": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000255", "source": "HAMAP-Rule", "id": "MF_01416"}], "value": "Peripheral membrane protein", "id": "SL-9903"}}]}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000255", "source": "HAMAP-Rule", "id": "MF_01416"}], "value": "Belongs to the ATPase delta chain family"}], "commentType": "SIMILARITY"}], "features": [{"type": "Chain", "location": {"start": {"value": 1, "modifier": "EXACT"}, "end": {"value": 183, "modifier": "EXACT"}}, "description": "ATP synthase subunit delta", "featureId": "PRO_0000371182"}], "keywords": [{"id": "KW-0066", "category": "Biological process", "name": "ATP synthesis"}, {"id": "KW-0997", "category": "Cellular component", "name": "Cell inner membrane"}, {"id": "KW-1003", "category": "Cellular component", "name"